Wizard Summary:  
  Magicbane uses dagger skill.  Magicbane is guaranteed.  Magicbane does
reliable damage.  Daggers are guaranteed.  Expert daggers do reliable damage
that beats every artifact weapon, except Grayswandir against silver hating
monsters.  Wielding Magicbane gives Magic Resistance and 95% curse absorption.
Magicbane does not destroy resources.  Magicbane at +7 for a wizard beats a
number of other artifacts against demons.

  If you want to do damage with a weapon, Expert thrown daggers are the obvious
choice for Wizards.  That skill carries over to Magicbane, a wizard's guaranteed
first gift.  

  For magic resistance, Wizards have a three layer defense: Cloak of MR, 
Eye of Aethiopica, wielded Magicbane.

  For doing damage, Wizards have a multi-layer approach as well:  Thrown
daggers, Elbereth engraved with Magicbane, wielded +7 Magicbane.  Attack spells
can be thrown in for tough monsters, especially at range. (or when at max mana).
It requires more preparation, thought, and effort.  Playing a wizard is not for
the hard of thinking.  The "Run up so the monster can hit me" approach is
sub-optimal.


