  The main thing is not to rely on spellcasting for attack.  Expert thrown
daggers are up there with the most powerful weapons in the game.  (And I don't
mean artifacts when I say powerful weapons.  Artifact weapons are mostly traps
set by the DevTeam to catch too-trusting players.  Just like #twoweaponing.)

  There are a lot of other spell schools, learn how to use them to save mana.

  Once you start using other spells intelligently you'll save a lot of mana.
Well-timed spells of charm monster can easily make your game.  Skilled+ Detect
Monsters keeps you from being taken by surprise.  It also acts like tracking
Radar for ranged attacks.  (That's why Rangers can get to skilled in
divination.)

  Getting to XL 30 not only gives you more mana, it makes spells more efficient.
Up to twice as efficient for some attack spells.  Going to skilled+ XL 30 cone
of cold is 80x as effective as unskilled/basic XL 15 cone of cold.  (9 squares
instead of 1, 4.5 hits per square instead of one, double the damage per hit.)


